es like Mastercard [Data: Entities (11, 261, 207); Relationships (318)]. Such innovations ensure BLIK remains competitive in the rapidly evolving digital payment market [Data: Entities (11, 261, 207)].\"\n        }\n    ]\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": [], "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}}], "created": 1748736296, "model": "gpt-4o-2024-08-06", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": "default", "system_fingerprint": "fp_a288987b44", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 827, "prompt_tokens": 7777, "total_tokens": 8604, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 1408}}}, "input": {"messages": [{"content": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            },\n            {\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }\n        ]\n    }\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\nLimit the total report length to 2000 words.\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n11,BLIK,\"BLIK is a Polish mobile payment system that has been operational since February 9, 2015. It was developed through a collaboration between the National Clearing House and six major banks: Alior Bank, Bank Millennium, BZ WBK, mBank, ING Bank Śląski, and PKO BP. Managed by the company Polski Standard Płatności, BLIK has quickly become the most frequently used mobile payment system in Poland, particularly popular among Generation Y and Z consumers.\n\nBLIK offers a wide range of functionalities, including quick internet transfers, contactless payments, phone transfers, BLIK checks, and ATM cash deposits and withdrawals. It allows users to make payments without the need for a physical card by generating a one-time six-digit code through a mobile banking app, which is valid for two minutes. This system facilitates various types of transactions such as online payments, POS terminal payments, P2P transfers, and in-store payments using codes. Since September 2021, BLIK has also supported contactless payments, further enhancing its usability in retail environments.\n\nThe system has seen significant growth in transaction numbers and value, particularly during the COVID-19 pandemic, when there was a marked increase in non-cash internet payments and P2P transfers. BLIK's rapid adoption is attributed to its integration with mobile banking applications and its competitive edge against other payment systems like Apple Pay and Google Pay.\n\nBLIK is available to users of mobile banking applications and is supported by several banks in Poland. It has become a dominant force in online shopping payments and is known for its innovative payment solutions, which include facilitating cashless transactions and offering a high transaction growth rate. Despite facing challenges such as limited user acceptance in stationary stores and competition from other payment providers, BLIK continues to be a leading mobile payment system in Poland, with a strong presence in both online and offline commerce.\",51\r\n28,ALIOR BANK,\"Alior Bank is a prominent financial institution based in Poland, known for its comprehensive range of mobile banking services and innovative payment solutions. Established as a forward-thinking bank, Alior Bank launched its mobile application in 2010, marking its commitment to digital transformation and customer convenience. The bank offers a variety of mobile banking login methods, including PIN, fingerprint, and face scan, ensuring secure and easy access for its users.\n\nDespite its innovative offerings, Alior Bank has been noted to have lower than average mobile banking indicators. However, it is part of a group with a high percentage of 'mobile only' users, indicating a strong focus on mobile banking solutions. This focus is further exemplified by its extensive mobile payment systems, which include BLIK, Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, Fitbit Pay, and Swatch PAY!, catering to a wide range of customer preferences and enhancing the ease of transactions.\n\nAlior Bank has been a key player in the development and implementation of the BLIK payment system, a significant milestone in Poland's banking sector. As one of the six banks involved in the creation of BLIK, Alior Bank has been offering these services since 2015. BLIK services provided by the bank include contactless payments and other functionalities, demonstrating Alior Bank's commitment to providing cutting-edge financial solutions to its customers.\n\nIn summary, Alior Bank stands out as a dynamic and innovative bank in Poland, offering a robust suite of mobile banking and payment services. Its involvement in the creation and promotion of the BLIK payment system highlights its role as a leader in the digital banking landscape, despite facing challenges with mobile banking indicators. Through its diverse payment options and secure mobile access methods, Alior Bank continues to enhance the banking experience for its customers, solidifying its position in the Polish financial market.\",6\r\n198,PEKAO,\"PEKAO is one of the major banks in Poland, recognized for its comprehensive mobile banking services. As a prominent financial institution, PEKAO has been at the forefront of integrating advanced technology into its banking operations, providing customers with a variety of convenient mobile banking login methods. These include the use of a PIN, fingerprint recognition, and face scan, ensuring both security and ease of access for its users.\n\nSince 2018, PEKAO has also been offering BLIK services, a popular mobile payment system in Poland, further enhancing its digital banking capabilities. This service allows customers to make quick and secure transactions using their mobile devices, reflecting the bank's commitment to innovation and customer convenience.\n\nPEKAO's mobile application has been a subject of analysis for its usage metrics, indicating a focus on understanding and improving user engagement and satisfaction. As part of a group with moderate mobile banking indicators, PEKAO continues to strive for excellence in its digital offerings, aiming to meet the evolving needs of its clientele.\n\nOverall, PEKAO stands out as a key player in the Polish banking sector, leveraging technology to provide efficient and secure banking solutions to its customers.\",5\r\n24,SANTANDER BANK POLSKA,\"Santander Bank Polska, formerly known as Wielkopolski Bank Kredytowy, is a prominent financial institution in Poland. The bank has established itself as a leader in the development and provision of mobile banking services, catering to the evolving needs of its customers. Santander Bank Polska offers a comprehensive suite of mobile payment systems, including BLIK, Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, and Fitbit Pay, ensuring that customers have access to a wide range of convenient and secure payment options. The bank's support for BLIK services is particularly noteworthy, as it includes functionalities such as contactless payments, which enhance the ease and efficiency of transactions for its users. Through its commitment to innovation and customer service, Santander Bank Polska continues to play a significant role in the Polish banking sector.\",4\r\n212,PAY-BY-LINK,Pay-by-link is a payment system that was surpassed by BLIK in terms of transaction numbers and value during the pandemic,2\r\n260,KRAJOWA IZBA ROZLICZENIOWA,\"Krajowa Izba Rozliczeniowa, also known as the National Clearing House, is a prominent organization in Poland that plays a significant role in the financial sector. It is actively involved in conducting research on consumer payment behaviors, providing valuable insights into how individuals in Poland manage and execute their financial transactions. This research helps in understanding trends and shifts in consumer preferences, which can influence the development of new financial products and services.\n\nIn addition to its research activities, Krajowa Izba Rozliczeniowa is a key player in the development of the BLIK payment system, a widely used mobile payment solution in Poland. The BLIK system allows users to make payments using their mobile devices, offering a convenient and secure method for conducting transactions. This system has become an integral part of the Polish payment landscape, reflecting the organization's commitment to advancing financial technology and improving the efficiency of payment processes in the country.\n\nThrough its dual focus on research and technological development, Krajowa Izba Rozliczeniowa contributes significantly to the modernization of Poland's financial infrastructure, supporting both consumers and businesses in adapting to the evolving digital economy.\",2\r\n262,SGB,\"SGB is a financial institution based in Poland, recognized for its commitment to enhancing mobile banking security. As a bank, SGB provides its customers with convenient and secure mobile banking login methods, including the use of PINs and fingerprint authentication, ensuring a seamless and protected user experience. Since 2021, SGB has also been offering BLIK services, a popular mobile payment system in Poland, further expanding its range of digital banking solutions. Through these offerings, SGB demonstrates its dedication to integrating advanced technology into its services, catering to the evolving needs of its clientele in the digital age.\",2\r\n13,BEATA ŚWIECKA,Professor Beata Świecka is a reviewer who provided valuable feedback during the editorial review of the monograph,1\r\n261,PSP,\"PSP is a company that plays a pivotal role in the development and expansion of the BLIK payment system. It collaborates closely with BLIK to enhance its functionalities, with a particular focus on advancing contactless payment solutions. PSP is responsible for introducing innovative features to the BLIK system, such as enabling payments without the need to enter a code and facilitating recurring payments. Through these efforts, PSP aims to streamline and improve the user experience, making BLIK a more versatile and user-friendly payment option.\",1\r\n272,REVOLUT,\"Revolut is a financial technology company that offers banking services including a prepaid debit card, currency exchange, and peer-to-peer payments.\",1\r\n273,RAIFFEISEN POLBANK,A bank that adopted BLIK in 2018,1\r\n274,BANK PEKAO SA,A bank that adopted BLIK in 2018,1\r\n275,BŁACH,Błach is an author mentioned in the context of discussing internal factors affecting BLIK's development,1\r\n276,CZYŻAK,Czyżak is an author mentioned in the context of discussing cybercrime in mobile banking,1\r\n73,NOBLE BANK,\"Noble Bank is a financial institution based in Poland, known for its comprehensive range of mobile payment systems. Since 2019, the bank has been offering BLIK services, a popular mobile payment solution in Poland. In addition to BLIK, Noble Bank supports a variety of other mobile payment platforms, including Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, and Xiaomi Pay. This diverse array of payment options underscores Noble Bank's commitment to providing its customers with convenient and flexible financial services, catering to the growing demand for digital and mobile banking solutions.\",2\r\n186,MOBILE BANKING APPLICATIONS,\"Mobile banking applications are software platforms provided by banks that enable customers to conduct a wide range of financial transactions and access various banking services through their mobile devices. These applications are designed to offer convenience and flexibility, allowing users to manage their finances on-the-go without the need to visit a physical bank branch. By leveraging the capabilities of mobile technology, these applications provide a secure and efficient means for customers to perform essential banking activities such as checking account balances, transferring funds, paying bills, and even depositing checks remotely. Additionally, mobile banking applications often include features that enhance the user experience, such as personalized notifications, budgeting tools, and access to customer support. As a result, they have become an integral part of modern banking, offering a seamless and user-friendly interface that caters to the evolving needs of tech-savvy consumers.\",12\r\n242,MILLENNIUM BANK,\"Millennium Bank is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized for its comprehensive range of mobile banking services. As a significant player in the Polish banking sector, Millennium Bank provides its customers with innovative and convenient banking solutions, including the popular BLIK services. BLIK is a mobile payment system that allows users to make transactions quickly and securely using their smartphones, reflecting the bank's commitment to integrating advanced technology into its service offerings. Millennium Bank's focus on mobile banking highlights its dedication to meeting the evolving needs of its customers by providing accessible and efficient financial services.\",3\r\n36,ING BANK ŚLĄSKI,\"ING Bank Śląski is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized for its leadership in mobile banking services. Established as one of the top five banks in the country by client numbers, ING Bank Śląski has consistently demonstrated innovation in the digital banking sector. The bank was a pioneer in offering mobile banking applications, launching its first app in 2012. It was notably the first Polish bank to introduce a mobile banking application specifically designed for tablets, showcasing its commitment to technological advancement and customer convenience.\n\nA key player in the development of mobile payment systems, ING Bank Śląski was one of the six banks involved in the creation of the BLIK payment system, which has become a widely used service in Poland. Since 2015, the bank has been providing BLIK services to its customers, enabling them to perform contactless payments and other functionalities with ease. In addition to BLIK, ING Bank Śląski offers a range of mobile payment options, including HCE, Google Pay, Apple Pay, and Garmin Pay, catering to the diverse needs of its tech-savvy clientele.\n\nThe bank's involvement in the Polish Standard of Payments further underscores its role in shaping the country's digital payment landscape. With a significant number of mobile banking users and high mobilization indicators, ING Bank Śląski continues to lead in the adoption and implementation of cutting-edge banking technologies. Its comprehensive suite of mobile banking services not only enhances customer experience but also solidifies its position as a forward-thinking institution in the competitive Polish banking market.\",7\r\n41,POLSKI STANDARD PŁATNOŚCI,\"Polski Standard Płatności is a company that was established in 2013 by a consortium of six banks with the primary objective of managing and coordinating the development of the BLIK mobile payment system in Poland. As the entity responsible for overseeing the BLIK project, Polski Standard Płatności plays a crucial role in the advancement and management of this innovative payment system within the country. The BLIK system, under the stewardship of Polski Standard Płatności, has become a significant player in the Polish financial landscape, offering a convenient and secure mobile payment solution to users. Through its efforts, Polski Standard Płatności continues to enhance the functionality and reach of BLIK, ensuring it meets the evolving needs of consumers and remains at the forefront of mobile payment technology in Poland.\",7\r\n40,PKO BP,\"PKO BP, also known as IKO, is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized for its extensive mobile banking services. As one of the six banks involved in the creation of the BLIK payment system, PKO BP has been offering BLIK services since 2015, which include contactless payments and other functionalities. The bank is a key player in the Polish Standard of Payments and has introduced the IKO mobile payment system, further solidifying its position in the mobile banking sector.\n\nWith a strong focus on digital innovation, PKO BP has developed a robust mobile banking platform that caters to a large customer base. The bank boasts 3.91 million active mobile app users and serves a total of 10.54 million individual clients. This highlights its significant presence in the Polish banking industry and its commitment to providing convenient and efficient banking solutions to its customers.\n\nPKO BP's mobile application usage metrics have been analyzed, indicating its role as a major bank in Poland with moderate mobile banking indicators. The bank's mobile services are well-regarded, and it continues to enhance its offerings to meet the evolving needs of its clients. As a leading bank in Poland, PKO BP remains dedicated to delivering high-quality financial services and maintaining its reputation as a trusted and innovative banking institution.\",6\r\n241,BLUE MEDIA,Blue Media is a company offering automatic toll payments on highways through the Autopay service,1\r\n195,COVID-19 PANDEMIC,\"The COVID-19 pandemic, a global health crisis that began in 2020, had far-reaching impacts on various aspects of life worldwide, including significant changes in consumer behavior and payment trends. In Poland, the pandemic led to the declaration of a state of epidemic, prompting administrative changes across retail and service sectors. These changes included the imposition of restrictions and a strong promotion of cashless payments to minimize physical contact and curb the spread of the virus.\n\nAs a result, there was a notable shift towards cashless transactions, with a marked increase in the use of online and mobile banking services. This shift was particularly evident among older generations, who traditionally relied more on cash but began adopting digital payment methods during the pandemic. The popularity of online shopping surged as physical trade faced restrictions, further driving the demand for payment cards and digital payment systems.\n\nOne of the significant outcomes of this shift was the increased usage of BLIK, a mobile payment system, especially among the oldest consumer group. The pandemic acted as a catalyst for the adoption of such technologies, as consumers sought safer and more convenient ways to conduct transactions without physical interaction.\n\nOverall, the COVID-19 pandemic not only altered consumer behavior but also accelerated the digital transformation of payment systems, highlighting the importance of adaptability in the face of unprecedented global challenges.\",9\r\n207,MASTERCARD,\"Mastercard is a global payment technology company that has been proactive in adapting to the evolving needs of its users, particularly during the COVID-19 pandemic. In response to the increased demand for safer and more convenient payment methods, Mastercard increased the contactless transaction limit. This strategic move was aimed at reducing the need for PIN entry, thereby minimizing physical contact and enhancing the safety and convenience of transactions during the pandemic.\n\nIn addition to its efforts to improve transaction safety, Mastercard has also been active in expanding its technological capabilities through strategic partnerships. In 2019, Mastercard partnered with PSP to enhance BLIK's contactless payment capabilities. This collaboration was part of Mastercard's broader strategy to innovate and improve the efficiency and reach of its payment solutions, ensuring that users have access to seamless and advanced payment technologies.\n\nThrough these initiatives, Mastercard has demonstrated its commitment to providing secure, efficient, and innovative payment solutions on a global scale.\",2\r\n196,TRADITIONAL PAYMENT CARDS,\"Traditional payment cards were the most popular form of payment during the pandemic, although their demand was affected by the rise of online shopping and the introduction of contactless systems like BLIK\",1\r\n205,MINISTRY OF DEVELOPMENT,The Ministry of Development issued recommendations to limit COVID-19 transmission in retail outlets,1\r\n206,VISA,Visa increased the contactless transaction limit to reduce the need for PIN entry during the COVID-19 pandemic,1\r\n190,SANTANDER BANK,\"Santander Bank, formerly known as Bank Zachodni WBK, is one of the largest banks in Poland. It is renowned for its substantial client base and leadership in mobile banking services. As a major financial institution in the country, Santander Bank has established a strong presence in the banking sector, offering a wide range of services to meet the diverse needs of its customers. The bank's commitment to innovation and customer service has positioned it as a leader in the industry, particularly in the realm of digital and mobile banking solutions.\",2\r\n27,RAIFFEISEN BANK POLSKA,\"Raiffeisen Bank Polska is a bank that launched a Java-based mobile application \"\"R-Mobile\"\" in 2004 and was the first to offer a mobile app on iOS in 2009\",2\r\n35,ALIOR SYNC,\"Alior Sync is a digital banking service that was launched by Alior Bank in 2012. It played a significant role in the early stages of mobile banking in Poland. As a pioneering initiative, Alior Sync provided mobile banking applications that allowed users to manage their finances conveniently through their smartphones. Over time, Alior Sync became an integral part of Alior Bank, contributing to the bank's reput